    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110-a1">

                <pb facs="0223" n="119" sameAs="frus:frus1890/pg119"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 197.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bernhard to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-09-22"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 22,
                        1890</date>. (Received October 17.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 99.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Respectfully, I inclose copies of telegrams
                    exchanged between this consulate and the legation of the United States of
                    America at Guatemala.</p>
                <p>The cable line is still closed, and the damages caused to the American
                    enterprises through the interruption of cables are countless.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. Bernhard</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Vice-Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
